# Description

See Alex's implementation at https://github.com/GalloDaSballo/twap-study
@GalloDaSballo any more notes to add

The purpose of the TWAP is to have a trailing average of the eBTC totalDebt value
This value is used in redemptions to determine the rate. The more that gets redeemed relative to the totalDebt, the higher the rate goes

(someone could use flashloans to inflate the debt temporarily and push the redemption fee down)

let's imagine a theoretical worst-case where the fee stays flat at 0.5% - then we've got a constant-sum AMM

of course that wouldn't happen but this is designed to reduce spot manipulation of the totalDebt value

in this case, we now take the lower of the TWAP value and the spot value. (so the fee scales faster than spot, in the case of the supply going up "naturally" or via flashloan)


## Known Issues
Until observed once, no redemptions are possible due to:

### Zero TWAP
When no time passes or observation has happened, it  leads to a div0 error, bricking redemptions.
In our case it’s considered the specification of the system that redemptions won’t be on for a while, so this is ok.
This is easy to resolve manually by taking a second CDP action or manually observing after some time.

> question: use totalDebt if TWAP reports zero? should we guard against this? @rayeaster @GalloDaSballo 
we could for example throw out a zero value and use spot. or just accept it.


example fix:
```solidity
function _openTestCDP(address _user, uint256 _coll, uint256 _debt) internal returns (bytes32) {
        dealCollateral(_user, _coll);
        vm.startPrank(_user);
        collateral.approve(address(borrowerOperations), type(uint256).max);
        bytes32 _cdpId = borrowerOperations.openCdp(_debt, bytes32(0), bytes32(0), _coll);
        vm.stopPrank();

        // TWAP must be non-zero for redemptions at system start
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1);
        activePool.update();

        return _cdpId;
    }
```
(note that this was reverted for final testing PR - all legacy tests advance the TWAP to equal spot)

# Test Fix Notes
### Echidna to Foundry Tests
These sequences are based on the old assumption of using the spot totalDebt.

There is now a convenience function in BaseFixture and corresponding Echdina setup
```solidity
function _syncSystemDebtTwapToSpotValue() internal {
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + activePool.PERIOD());
        activePool.update();
    }
```

note that each setUp() empirically resets timestamp at `1`

TODO: How to dedup? `BaseStorageVariables -> BaseFunctions`

### Broken Tests
Some tests remain broken due to a new issue I haven't explored yet.

## Additional Tests
- Implement Alex's tests from https://github.com/GalloDaSballo/twap-study

This is a follow-up to 5e39a36.  Fix two oversights:

- Some bug in conditional causes three-valued and five-valued (specifically!) cases to be skipped;

- Unwrapping of `values` without checking for single-valuedness can lead to unsound optimization.

